caption: Caps and Special Mechanics
engine-rule: caps-and-special-mechanics

The universal Atavistic Engine grants no Power Talent, governing Talent, Strong/Tough/Fast emphasis, attribute formula, DR, Extra Attack, movement allowance, natural attack, Super-Effort, Alternate Form, Morph, ATR, Unkillable, Regeneration, or other generic advantage. Those are implementation-specific permissions.

Each Atavistic Tradition must state every relevant attribute cap, Size Modifier limit, DR cap, Extra Attack cap, movement cap, natural-attack cap, major leveled-trait cap, mandatory modifier, visible feature, weakness, prerequisite, and exception needed by its own Source system. A Domain-specific Talent, Path, transformation, equipment host, acquisition rule, or other mechanic may modify those permissions only when the Tradition explicitly says so.
